---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---
<Page
  title="About · yokoten doctor"
  description="yokoten doctor is a free page that checks a public GitHub repo for the files AI agents need. How a check runs, its limits, and how this page was made."
  path="/about.html"
>
<Header />
<main id="top" class="section-inner about">
  <h1>About yokoten doctor</h1>
  <p class="about-lede">A free page that checks a public GitHub repo for the files AI agents need. Paste a URL and read the result in your browser. No terminal needed.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>What you get back</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>13 file checks, and where the repo stands.</li>
      <li>The one thing to fix next.</li>
      <li>Files written for your repo, ready to commit.</li>
      <li>The commands to run the same check yourself.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How a check runs</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>You paste a public GitHub repo URL.</li>
      <li>A throwaway sandbox copies the repo, then its network is cut.</li>
      <li><code>yokoten</code> reads the copy. Your code never runs: no install, no build, no tests.</li>
      <li>The server sends some of the repo's files to Muse Spark Open, on Baseten. Muse writes the “This project” section of <code>AGENTS.md</code>.</li>
      <li>You get the result and the files. Nothing changes until you commit on GitHub.</li>
      <li>The server writes a hash of the result to Sigstore Rekor and a Solana devnet memo. Devnet is a test network, so nothing on it has real value.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Public repos only.</li>
      <li>It doesn't scan your code for vulnerabilities.</li>
      <li>A very large repo may not finish in time.</li>
      <li>Five of the 13 checks only pass once <code>yokoten</code> is installed, so a repo without it tops out at 8 of 13.</li>
      <li>Muse's text stays in a cache for 24 hours.</li>
      <li>It's free, with no account. Each visitor gets 10 checks an hour.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="about-made">
    <h2>How this was made</h2>
    <dl>
      <div>
        <dt>Muse Spark Open</dt>
        <dd>Most of the code, and each repo's project section</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Claude Fable 5.1</dt>
        <dd>This site's visual design and its copy</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Claude Opus 5.5</dt>
        <dd>The first design, task briefs, code review, and some later changes by hand</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>yokoten</dt>
        <dd>The checks and the logo. It started before this project, and it's still growing</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p>The full note is in the <a href="https://github.com/coo1white/yokoten-doctor#disclosure">README</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Something wrong?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A wrong check result belongs in the <a href="https://github.com/yokoten-labs/yokoten/issues">yokoten repo</a>. The checks are yokoten's; this page only shows them.</li>
      <li>A broken page belongs in <a href="https://github.com/coo1white/yokoten-doctor/issues">this repo</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</main>
<Footer />
</Page>
